# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Dev-generated keys and certificates (never commit secrets)
**/keys/
**/*.pem
**/*.pub
**/*.key

# SQLite databases generated at runtime
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Service logs written by dev.sh. Every example run rewrites these, so tracking
# them meant `git status` was never clean and the build-host guard could not tell
# real uncommitted work from a stack having been started once.
**/logs/
# ...but keep the directory itself. Example 08 is the log viewer: m6-file serves
# a route rooted at logs/, so on a fresh clone the directory has to exist.
!**/logs/.gitkeep

# macOS
.DS_Store

# ...and keep the CMS drafts directory. git does not track empty directories, so
# without this a fresh clone has no content/drafts/ and render-cms's dashboard
# 500'd on it. The handler tolerates the absence now too; both, because a reader
# should not depend on either alone.
!examples/05-cms/content/drafts/.gitkeep
